 "_about": "Warehouse 126 (the owner, 2026-11-22) and the owner's decision of 2026-11-25 on the font question (\"א. צריך שיהיה את כל המגוון\", DECISIONS.md): a library of font pairs, so a page never gets a font the model invented, never Heebo everywhere, and different businesses get different, fitting pairs. A content-only site's customer is not asked which font (omni_prod/discovery.fonts_by_platform): 148AI picks the pair. Per supported script (scripts.json) a range of pairs -- at least MIN_PAIRS_PER_TONE (omni_prod/typography) for every tone -- each a display face for headings and a body face. 'families' is the allowed list: every family a pair names, with its licence as google/fonts METADATA.pb states it (OFL, the SIL Open Font License, or APACHE2, Apache 2.0), its Google Fonts categories and classifications, the library scripts its subsets cover, and the weights fonts.googleapis.com/css2 serves in its script's subset, each read live on the date given. A family not listed, under another licence, without its script or missing a weight, a display face set as body text, or a listed family no pair uses fails the import; tests/test_font_pair_range_live.py reads the licences and the served weights live again and renders every Hebrew pair on the section library's page, and tests/test_font_pairs_load.py loads every pair in Chromium. Each face loads the design contract's two weights, 400 and 700, or 400 alone for a single-weight display face. 'tones' are the section library's art directions (directions.json): a business's category gives its palette, the palette its direction, and the direction the pairs it may get; the business itself (its name, with its category) picks one of them, the same every time (omni_prod/typography.pair_for). Formal and elegant pages get a serif or a sober display face, warm pages a rounded, handwritten or friendly one, bold pages a heavy or condensed one; the body is always a text face. No family belongs to two scripts, so a Hebrew page and an Arabic page never share a font.",
